WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:00:00.020 --> 00:00:05.860
<b>Navy Headquarters
New World</b>

3
00:00:12.420 --> 00:00:15.760
[AKAINU]
I bet you're
oh-so happy, Issho.

4
00:00:15.760 --> 00:00:17.920
You've been pushing
for this forever.

5
00:00:17.920 --> 00:00:19.630
Well, you got your wish!

6
00:00:19.630 --> 00:00:22.260
The Seven Warlords
have been abolished.

7
00:00:22.260 --> 00:00:24.850
You know I stood
firmly against it!

8
00:00:24.850 --> 00:00:26.890
But when the guys at
the top make the call,

9
00:00:26.890 --> 00:00:28.680
there's no reversin' it!

10
00:00:28.680 --> 00:00:31.190
They should know that
justice comes with a price tag.

11
00:00:31.190 --> 00:00:33.310
Who do you think is
paying that price?

12
00:00:33.310 --> 00:00:34.690
Take a step back!

13
00:00:36.520 --> 00:00:40.400
A pity. Still can't see
the bigger picture, can you?

14
00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:42.490
It's 'cause you've never been
one of the innocent folks

15
00:00:42.490 --> 00:00:45.410
this cruel world has
chewed up and spit out.

16
00:00:45.410 --> 00:00:49.660
Happens every day
to good people.

17
00:00:49.660 --> 00:00:52.000
Hurry up! We don't have time!
Keep moving!

18
00:01:06.680 --> 00:01:09.770
The Seven Warlords
are now no more.

19
00:01:09.770 --> 00:01:11.390
Things are gonna
get a bit rocky,

20
00:01:11.390 --> 00:01:15.440
so we'll need to put our trust
in our Special Science Group.

21
00:01:17.020 --> 00:01:18.730
The power balance
in this world is

22
00:01:18.730 --> 00:01:22.070
about to be turned
completely upside down.

23
00:01:23.110 --> 00:01:27.410
That's not the only thing
upside down right now.

24
00:01:27.410 --> 00:01:29.910
Word has it that
Kaido and Big Mom

25
00:01:29.910 --> 00:01:32.080
are joining forces in Wano.

26
00:01:32.080 --> 00:01:34.620
[FUJITORA]
Hm? That can't be!

27
00:01:35.990 --> 00:01:39.160
<b>Issho</b>

28
00:01:36.130 --> 00:01:39.760
[FUJITORA]
The legendary
Rocks Pirates have returned?

29
00:01:39.760 --> 00:01:41.720
[roars]

30
00:01:46.180 --> 00:01:48.470
[AKAINU]
Nothing "legendary"
about this mess.

31
00:01:48.470 --> 00:01:50.260
It's as real as it gets.

32
00:01:50.260 --> 00:01:53.440
And it's our problem
to deal with.

33
00:01:53.440 --> 00:01:56.480
Unfortunately, they don't
care how busy we are.

34
00:01:56.480 --> 00:01:59.900
They're just the latest
fiasco on our plate!

35
00:02:01.320 --> 00:02:05.450
[MARINE C]
Two Emperors
of the Sea teamed up?

36
00:02:05.450 --> 00:02:06.540
There's no way!

37
00:02:06.540 --> 00:02:08.580
They're really
pulling this right now?

38
00:02:08.580 --> 00:02:09.870
[BRANNEW]
Well, technically speaking,

39
00:02:09.870 --> 00:02:13.420
the intel reports they're
"about to" unite.

40
00:02:13.420 --> 00:02:15.590
There's been no damages
as of this moment,

41
00:02:15.590 --> 00:02:17.170
but we don't understand
their motives

42
00:02:17.170 --> 00:02:19.130
or how to handle this yet.

43
00:02:19.130 --> 00:02:23.010
We only have a single detail
confirmed at this current time.

44
00:02:23.010 --> 00:02:25.680
They both hail from
the notorious Rocks Pirates.

45
00:02:25.680 --> 00:02:27.220
[Marines gasp]

46
00:02:27.220 --> 00:02:32.270
Though actual details on the
Rocks crew are fairly sparse.

47
00:02:32.270 --> 00:02:33.730
Big Mom and Kaido have been

48
00:02:33.730 --> 00:02:36.150
at odds with one
another for ages.

49
00:02:36.150 --> 00:02:38.110
So, this is coming
out of left field.

50
00:02:38.110 --> 00:02:40.650
Can't say I could've
predicted this one.

51
00:02:40.650 --> 00:02:43.360
If I may, who are
the Rocks Pirates?

52
00:02:43.360 --> 00:02:45.370
[SENGOKU]
Ah, of course.

53
00:02:45.370 --> 00:02:46.700
You wouldn't know
much about them

54
00:02:46.700 --> 00:02:49.900
since they came
long before your time.

55
00:02:49.900 --> 00:02:51.660
[SENGOKU]
The Rocks Pirates were a gang of

56
00:02:51.660 --> 00:02:53.820
extremely dangerous individuals

57
00:02:53.820 --> 00:02:57.330
who came together on
the Pirate Island of Fullalead.

58
00:02:57.330 --> 00:02:59.700
Their entire allegiance
was founded

59
00:02:59.700 --> 00:03:02.790
in order to make one big score.

60
00:03:06.460 --> 00:03:08.760
[SENGOKU]
They were such
a vicious bunch of scoundrels

61
00:03:08.760 --> 00:03:11.970
that they'd often kill
their own crewmates.

62
00:03:14.300 --> 00:03:18.850
[SENGOKU]
Captain Rocks' lineup
consisted of many heavy hitters.

63
00:03:20.180 --> 00:03:22.940
[SENGOKU]
This included Whitebeard...

64
00:03:25.150 --> 00:03:27.070
[SENGOKU]
...Big Mom...

65
00:03:29.070 --> 00:03:30.900
[SENGOKU]
...and Kaido.

66
00:03:30.900 --> 00:03:33.910
[Marines chattering]

67
00:03:33.910 --> 00:03:36.700
I know that it's hard
to believe, but trust me.

68
00:03:36.700 --> 00:03:39.370
They were all once a part
of the same pirate crew!

69
00:03:37.330 --> 00:03:39.540
[Marines gasp]

70
00:03:39.540 --> 00:03:41.290
[MARINES]
– What?!
– What?!

71
00:03:43.420 --> 00:03:44.500
That's crazy!

72
00:03:44.500 --> 00:03:46.540
I can hardly
believe that's true!

73
00:03:46.540 --> 00:03:48.460
Amazingly enough,
those three weren't

74
00:03:48.460 --> 00:03:50.340
the only crew members
who went on

75
00:03:50.340 --> 00:03:52.590
to make a name for themselves.

76
00:03:52.590 --> 00:03:55.180
Just as an example, some of
their other prestigious members

77
00:03:55.180 --> 00:03:59.930
included Shiki the Golden Lion,
the Silver Axe,

78
00:03:59.930 --> 00:04:01.980
Captain John, and Wang Zhi.

79
00:04:01.980 --> 00:04:05.150
Seriously? All those maniacs
were on the same crew

80
00:04:05.150 --> 00:04:06.350
and they didn't
wipe each other out?

81
00:04:06.350 --> 00:04:09.440
But how can this story
be lost to history?

82
00:04:09.440 --> 00:04:12.190
If they hated their crewmates
that much, well,

83
00:04:12.190 --> 00:04:15.030
they wouldn't want
to tell their tale.

84
00:04:15.030 --> 00:04:19.030
Back then, Captain Rocks
was fighting to be

85
00:04:19.030 --> 00:04:21.160
"King of the World."

86
00:04:29.920 --> 00:04:32.170
[SENGOKU]
They were openly
hostile to the Government.

87
00:04:32.170 --> 00:04:35.010
They should have been
considered terrorists.

88
00:04:35.010 --> 00:04:36.880
But many of their incidents
were covered up

89
00:04:36.880 --> 00:04:38.680
because the truth
was discomforting

90
00:04:38.680 --> 00:04:41.180
and made us look weak.

91
00:04:41.180 --> 00:04:44.390
Not that it mattered,
but when they ruled the seas,

92
00:04:44.390 --> 00:04:47.190
everyone was well aware
of the threat they posed.

93
00:04:47.190 --> 00:04:47.690
[Marines gasp]

94
00:04:47.690 --> 00:04:49.110
Then the news broke out.

95
00:04:49.110 --> 00:04:52.990
The God Valley incident,
just 38 years ago.

96
00:04:53.520 --> 00:05:02.410
<b>38 Years Ago</b>

97
00:04:53.900 --> 00:04:55.410
According to the reports,

98
00:04:55.410 --> 00:04:58.580
the fiercest crew in the world,
the Rocks Pirates,

99
00:04:58.580 --> 00:05:02.620
had been completely
annihilated on that island.

100
00:05:02.620 --> 00:05:05.120
[Marines scream]

101
00:05:09.250 --> 00:05:12.010
[Rock Pirates yell]

102
00:05:32.780 --> 00:05:35.860
[Marines cheer]

103
00:05:36.780 --> 00:05:38.570
[SENGOKU]
That rampaging force of evil

104
00:05:38.570 --> 00:05:40.910
that no one was
able to stop before

105
00:05:40.910 --> 00:05:45.830
had been crushed by the
Navy Vice Admiral Garp.

106
00:05:46.870 --> 00:05:49.630
His name soon reached
the ends of the world.

107
00:05:49.630 --> 00:05:55.880
That day he became known as
"The great hero of the Navy"!

108
00:05:55.880 --> 00:05:57.380
I knew he was a badass,

109
00:05:57.380 --> 00:05:59.510
but I never heard
how he got that title.

110
00:05:59.510 --> 00:06:04.310
He's more than earned it!

111
00:06:04.310 --> 00:06:06.100
[MARINE N]
I've heard
a hundred tales of heroism

112
00:06:06.100 --> 00:06:08.140
about Vice Admiral Garp.

113
00:06:08.140 --> 00:06:11.690
It's hard to believe such an
important one went unnoticed.

114
00:06:11.690 --> 00:06:14.190
He's really taken on
all the bigshot pirates!

115
00:06:14.190 --> 00:06:16.240
And he won, no less!

116
00:06:19.070 --> 00:06:22.830
[sighs]
Big Mom and Kaido
have allied with each other?

117
00:06:22.830 --> 00:06:27.540
When can we catch a break?

118
00:06:27.540 --> 00:06:28.830
[SENGOKU]
You haven't heard much because

119
00:06:28.830 --> 00:06:31.340
the man himself
refuses to talk about it.

120
00:06:31.340 --> 00:06:33.200
[MARINE O]
Why's that?

121
00:06:33.200 --> 00:06:34.500
Even if he doesn't like it much,

122
00:06:34.500 --> 00:06:38.210
I'll tell you so the tale
isn't lost to history.

123
00:06:38.210 --> 00:06:39.540
There were two reasons why this

124
00:06:39.540 --> 00:06:41.920
was never reported
to the presses.

125
00:06:41.920 --> 00:06:44.880
The first being he had to
work alongside pirates

126
00:06:44.880 --> 00:06:47.050
in order to win the battle.

127
00:06:47.050 --> 00:06:49.220
– [Marines gasp]
– Are you joking?

128
00:06:49.220 --> 00:06:50.680
That's not everything.

129
00:06:50.680 --> 00:06:53.640
He protected the Celestial
Dragons in doing so.

130
00:06:53.640 --> 00:06:55.720
– [Marines gasp]
– [MARINE H] Hang on a moment!

131
00:06:55.720 --> 00:06:58.100
How do they
tie into all of this?

132
00:07:02.020 --> 00:07:03.400
So what?

133
00:07:03.400 --> 00:07:06.190
Isn't it the Navy's duty
to keep them safe though?

134
00:07:06.190 --> 00:07:08.530
I don't see a problem!

135
00:07:08.530 --> 00:07:10.280
[SENGOKU]
It's Garp's own moral compass

136
00:07:10.280 --> 00:07:12.350
that tells him otherwise.

137
00:07:12.350 --> 00:07:14.810
[SENGOKU]
A major reason why
he's refused the promotion

138
00:07:14.810 --> 00:07:16.900
to Admiral stems from
the fact that it would

139
00:07:16.900 --> 00:07:20.860
place him directly under
the Celestial Dragon's command.

140
00:07:20.860 --> 00:07:22.780
It's his accomplishments
and reputation

141
00:07:22.780 --> 00:07:26.820
that prevent him from being
dismissed for insubordination.

142
00:07:26.820 --> 00:07:28.910
Brace yourself
for the next part.

143
00:07:28.910 --> 00:07:31.950
Garp had to act quickly to
protect the Celestial Dragons

144
00:07:31.950 --> 00:07:33.830
and their slaves at God Valley.

145
00:07:33.830 --> 00:07:37.080
With no other options left,
he joined forces with Roger.

146
00:07:37.080 --> 00:07:38.750
Together, they pooled
their numbers

147
00:07:38.750 --> 00:07:41.170
to defeat the Rocks Pirates.

148
00:07:41.170 --> 00:07:44.510
That is the truth of
the God Valley Incident.

149
00:07:44.480 --> 00:07:45.940
<b>Retired</b>

150
00:07:44.510 --> 00:07:47.550
[Marines gasp]

151
00:07:47.550 --> 00:07:48.720
Like Gold Roger ?

152
00:07:48.720 --> 00:07:49.760
King of the Pirates?

153
00:07:49.760 --> 00:07:51.180
They fought together?

154
00:07:51.180 --> 00:07:54.520
Celestial Dragons, Gold Roger,
and the Rocks Pirates?

155
00:07:54.520 --> 00:07:56.850
You listed off
so many big names!

156
00:07:56.850 --> 00:07:59.820
Hard to believe all those people
were there at the same time!

157
00:07:59.820 --> 00:08:03.650
How have I not even heard of
this God Valley place?

158
00:08:03.650 --> 00:08:06.200
It's no surprise there.

159
00:08:07.070 --> 00:08:10.870
[SENGOKU]
Look for it on a modern-day map.

160
00:08:10.870 --> 00:08:14.240
You won't find that
island's name anywhere.

161
00:08:16.210 --> 00:08:18.670
[SENGOKU]
For good reason, too.

162
00:08:18.670 --> 00:08:21.460
It disappeared without a trace.

163
00:08:21.460 --> 00:08:25.220
[Marines gasp]

164
00:08:25.220 --> 00:08:27.090
[SENGOKU]
The Government
wanted to hide what happened

165
00:08:27.090 --> 00:08:30.300
on that island and
they made it disappear.

166
00:08:30.300 --> 00:08:34.430
Knowing this, do you still
want to hear more of the story?

167
00:08:34.430 --> 00:08:37.480
In the end, Rocks was thwarted
by his own ambition.

168
00:08:37.480 --> 00:08:39.560
He broke one too many taboos.

169
00:08:39.560 --> 00:08:41.020
The tales of his heinous crimes

170
00:08:41.020 --> 00:08:42.690
were deemed unfit
for the public,

171
00:08:42.690 --> 00:08:46.150
and so he came to exist
only in legend.

172
00:08:46.150 --> 00:08:46.700
[BOTH gasp]

173
00:08:46.700 --> 00:08:49.030
It is a legacy that only
lingers in the memories

174
00:08:49.030 --> 00:08:52.240
of a few old Marines
from my generation.

175
00:08:52.240 --> 00:08:55.410
It's hard to imagine it.
I know this was years ago,

176
00:08:55.410 --> 00:08:56.000
but it's crazy to think one man
led three of the Four Emperors.

177
00:08:56.000 --> 00:08:57.260
[REVOLUTIONARY D]
Crazy to think one of the

178
00:08:57.260 --> 00:08:58.970
Four Emperors is down.

179
00:08:59.250 --> 00:09:02.090
Captain Rocks was
Gold Roger's very first enemy

180
00:09:02.090 --> 00:09:05.090
and perhaps his
greatest one, as well.

181
00:09:05.090 --> 00:09:07.380
That aside, there was
something very interesting

182
00:09:07.380 --> 00:09:09.550
that those two had in common.

183
00:09:09.930 --> 00:09:11.340
Though it was rarely spoken,

184
00:09:11.340 --> 00:09:14.810
Rocks' full name was
Rocks D. Xebec.

185
00:09:14.810 --> 00:09:17.310
He had a special trait
some pirates share.

186
00:09:17.310 --> 00:09:19.230
That being the "D." initial.

187
00:09:19.230 --> 00:09:22.820
Although, he is no longer
alive to speak of it.

188
00:09:38.010 --> 00:09:41.970
<b>Retired</b>

189
00:09:38.390 --> 00:09:40.350
[SENGOKU]
It's true that
Kaido and Big Mom were

190
00:09:40.350 --> 00:09:43.850
once shipmates under
the same captain.

191
00:09:41.970 --> 00:09:43.890
<b>Retired</b>

192
00:09:43.850 --> 00:09:46.560
However, that was 38 years ago,

193
00:09:46.560 --> 00:09:49.480
and they were nothing like
they are at the present.

194
00:09:49.480 --> 00:09:51.520
If the intel that we
received is accurate,

195
00:09:51.520 --> 00:09:52.740
then this would be the birth of

196
00:09:52.740 --> 00:09:55.610
the most dangerous
pirate crew in the world.

197
00:09:55.610 --> 00:09:57.320
All right, Brannew,
why don't you tell us

198
00:09:57.320 --> 00:09:59.700
what everyone's
bounties will be.

199
00:09:59.700 --> 00:10:01.280
With pleasure, but keep in mind

200
00:10:01.280 --> 00:10:03.080
that we'll have to go back
to the drawing board

201
00:10:03.080 --> 00:10:04.700
on the bounties
for the Warlords,

202
00:10:04.700 --> 00:10:07.160
since they've had their
immunity stripped away.

203
00:10:07.160 --> 00:10:08.420
As for the other big shots,

204
00:10:08.420 --> 00:10:11.460
we can go over
their numbers easily.

205
00:10:15.160 --> 00:10:18.920
[grunts]

206
00:10:20.930 --> 00:10:23.020
Let's start with the
newest Emperor of the Sea

207
00:10:23.020 --> 00:10:25.520
who attained his title
about a year ago.

208
00:10:25.520 --> 00:10:27.940
I'm sure you know.

209
00:10:27.940 --> 00:10:29.940
He gained popularity
after his assault

210
00:10:29.940 --> 00:10:32.270
on Impel Down two years back.

211
00:10:32.270 --> 00:10:34.900
Now occupying the
Pirate Island Fullalead,

212
00:10:34.900 --> 00:10:38.030
he continues to expand
his territory and influence

213
00:10:38.030 --> 00:10:41.200
while filling the void that
Whitebeard left behind.

214
00:10:43.410 --> 00:10:45.660
[BRANNEW]
Commodore of
the Blackbeard Pirates.

215
00:10:45.660 --> 00:10:52.170
Marshall D. Teach!
2,247,600,000 berries!

216
00:10:52.170 --> 00:10:55.970
[Marines gasp]

217
00:10:56.800 --> 00:10:58.420
As for the next bounty.

218
00:10:58.420 --> 00:11:01.800
This man has been
an Emperor for six years now.

219
00:11:02.680 --> 00:11:03.970
He's the youngest of the four

220
00:11:03.970 --> 00:11:06.350
and deeply admired
by his subordinates,

221
00:11:06.350 --> 00:11:08.940
whom you probably have heard of.

222
00:11:08.940 --> 00:11:13.110
Beckman. Roux. Yasopp.

223
00:11:13.110 --> 00:11:15.530
Each with a high
average bounty themselves,

224
00:11:15.530 --> 00:11:17.320
this pirate crew is
world renowned for

225
00:11:17.320 --> 00:11:19.820
having an excellent
balance of skills.

226
00:11:19.820 --> 00:11:22.580
There really are
no weaklings amongst them.

227
00:11:23.240 --> 00:11:27.160
The chief of the Red-Hair
Pirates, Red-Haired Shanks!

228
00:11:27.160 --> 00:11:32.380
He's set at
4,048,900,000 berries!

229
00:11:32.380 --> 00:11:35.960
[Marines gasp]

230
00:11:35.960 --> 00:11:38.170
Now let's move on.

231
00:11:38.170 --> 00:11:39.550
She was born a monster,

232
00:11:39.550 --> 00:11:42.220
who allegedly destroyed
an entire village of Giants

233
00:11:42.220 --> 00:11:45.430
in Elbaph when she
was just a child.

234
00:11:46.180 --> 00:11:48.810
If you're not one of
her 85 children,

235
00:11:48.810 --> 00:11:50.390
or at least related by blood,

236
00:11:50.390 --> 00:11:53.230
you will naturally be
mistrusted by her.

237
00:11:53.230 --> 00:11:55.610
She's the undisputed
Queen of the sweet-themed

238
00:11:55.610 --> 00:11:58.900
network of islands
known as Totto Land!

239
00:11:59.610 --> 00:12:02.990
[BRANNEW]
That is of course the
captain of the Big Mom Pirates,

240
00:12:02.990 --> 00:12:04.450
Charlotte Linlin!

241
00:12:04.450 --> 00:12:08.410
She's worth
4,388,000,000 berries!

242
00:12:08.410 --> 00:12:11.870
[Marines gasp]

243
00:12:12.710 --> 00:12:14.840
Finally, we have
a monster who made

244
00:12:14.840 --> 00:12:17.960
a name for himself
early on in life.

245
00:12:17.960 --> 00:12:21.880
This man was only an apprentice
when he joined the Rocks crew.

246
00:12:22.800 --> 00:12:25.640
[BRANNEW]
He won the respect of
the most ferocious of pirates

247
00:12:25.640 --> 00:12:27.560
through his sheer strength alone

248
00:12:27.560 --> 00:12:32.140
until he was worthy of earning
the title Emperor of the Sea.

249
00:12:33.980 --> 00:12:36.440
[BRANNEW]
Supreme Commander
of the Beast Pirates,

250
00:12:36.440 --> 00:12:43.450
Kaido, King of the Beasts,
worth 4,611,100,000 berries!

251
00:12:47.620 --> 00:12:49.000
How distressing.

252
00:12:49.000 --> 00:12:51.120
Now, it goes without saying,

253
00:12:51.120 --> 00:12:53.250
but they decided at the Reverie

254
00:12:53.250 --> 00:12:58.420
that we will no longer have
the Warlords at our disposal.

255
00:12:58.420 --> 00:13:01.670
[grunts]

256
00:13:01.670 --> 00:13:04.220
Only time will tell
if distancing ourselves

257
00:13:04.220 --> 00:13:06.390
was a good decision or not.

258
00:13:06.390 --> 00:13:07.800
We'll have to wait and see how

259
00:13:07.800 --> 00:13:11.180
the Navy's Special Science Team,
the S.G., performs.

260
00:13:11.180 --> 00:13:14.560
Since we're here,
I'll put this in perspective.

261
00:13:14.560 --> 00:13:18.020
I might as well share the
bounties of some other legends.

262
00:13:19.690 --> 00:13:22.570
[BRANNEW]
The captain of
the Whitebeard Pirates,

263
00:13:22.570 --> 00:13:24.660
Edward Newgate!

264
00:13:24.660 --> 00:13:28.240
5,046,000,000 berries!

265
00:13:32.660 --> 00:13:34.790
[BRANNEW]
The captain
of the Roger Pirates,

266
00:13:34.790 --> 00:13:37.580
the King of the Pirates,
Gold Roger!

267
00:13:37.580 --> 00:13:42.460
5,564,800,000!

268
00:13:45.830 --> 00:13:48.540
[BRANNEW]
There hasn't been
a bounty to surpass these two.

269
00:13:48.540 --> 00:13:52.000
At least not yet!

270
00:13:54.590 --> 00:13:57.300
[BRANNEW]
But if Big Mom
and Kaido form their alliance,

271
00:13:57.300 --> 00:13:58.590
their combined bounty will be

272
00:13:58.590 --> 00:14:00.510
the highest the world
has ever seen,

273
00:14:00.510 --> 00:14:03.390
and the size of their
crew will be huge.

274
00:14:05.540 --> 00:14:06.830
[BRANNEW]
I've read the reports.

275
00:14:06.830 --> 00:14:09.790
This is happening
as we speak in Wano.

276
00:14:11.210 --> 00:14:12.920
[BRANNEW]
Fleet Admiral Sakazuki!

277
00:14:12.920 --> 00:14:15.130
We won't be getting
involved with that.

278
00:14:15.130 --> 00:14:18.010
[Marines gasp]

279
00:14:18.010 --> 00:14:19.510
In case you went senile,

280
00:14:19.510 --> 00:14:21.380
we lack the manpower
and resources

281
00:14:21.380 --> 00:14:23.390
to handle this currently!

282
00:14:23.390 --> 00:14:25.470
Any questions?

283
00:14:32.270 --> 00:14:35.820
None. I never intended
to get involved anyway.

284
00:14:35.820 --> 00:14:38.490
This old man was simply
providing these young soldiers

285
00:14:38.490 --> 00:14:41.110
with some wisdom and experience.

286
00:14:45.740 --> 00:14:49.000
[SENGOKU]
At the end of the day,
pirates are humans.

287
00:14:49.000 --> 00:14:51.790
They have their own
relationships and reasons.

288
00:14:51.790 --> 00:14:55.750
You can't take action
without knowing their history.

289
00:14:55.750 --> 00:14:57.260
Speaking of which.

290
00:14:57.260 --> 00:15:00.340
There was a pirate from Wano
who Whitebeard was fond of.

291
00:15:00.340 --> 00:15:03.840
He was favored by Roger
and Red-Hair.

292
00:15:03.840 --> 00:15:07.430
[Marines gasp]

293
00:15:07.430 --> 00:15:10.310
[AKAINU]
You mean
Kozuki Oden, don't you?

294
00:15:10.310 --> 00:15:11.730
The man who served
as a commander

295
00:15:11.730 --> 00:15:14.230
on Whitebeard's ship long ago.

296
00:15:14.230 --> 00:15:17.980
None other, of course.
And that's not all he did.

297
00:15:17.980 --> 00:15:19.650
The King of the Pirates
recruited him

298
00:15:19.650 --> 00:15:21.610
for his final journey.

299
00:15:21.610 --> 00:15:23.160
Something's not adding up.

300
00:15:23.160 --> 00:15:26.450
While I can't imagine Oden
being connected, it seems odd.

301
00:15:28.990 --> 00:15:30.500
[AKAINU]
Hm?

302
00:15:31.830 --> 00:15:33.330
[SENGOKU]
Doesn't it make you question why

303
00:15:33.330 --> 00:15:35.880
all these huge players
have such close ties

304
00:15:35.880 --> 00:15:39.340
to an isolated country
like the Land of Wano?

305
00:15:42.180 --> 00:15:44.550
[SENGOKU]
I can't believe
it's coincidence.

306
00:15:44.550 --> 00:15:49.140
You'd do well to keep
your eyes open, Sakazuki.
